{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>The fifth word [of the verse]</b><br>תורק. Feminine form (for שמן [oil], and if no parallel is found — like בית, which is masculine, and elsewhere feminine) as in כי שחה אל מות ביתה [for she sinks down to death her house], and likewise the word שאול." "<b>The third word [of the verse]</b><br>על כן עלמות אהבוך. [It is] ואת הנפש אשר עשו בחרן [and the soul that they made in Haran]."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The parenthetical reads as a note on grammatical gender fluidity; the internal quote is Proverbs 2:18.", 1 "The bracketed Hebrew citation is Genesis 12:5; Ibn Ezra read it as identifying the עלמות with the converts/souls acquired in Haran."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:48.381963466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}